-- Schema version 1 → 2: the activity trail.
--
-- ## Why this repo suddenly has migrations
-- Everything before this was additive-with-a-default on an EXISTING table
-- (`parentStationId`, `filterMode`, `viaStationId`, …), and `.sq` files are
-- applied in full to a fresh database — so a clean install always had the
-- current schema and the absence of migrations went unnoticed.
--
-- A NEW TABLE is where that stops working. `Schema.create` only ever runs on an
-- empty database, so without this file an install that already has
-- `stationly.db` never gets `ActivityEventEntity`, and the first enqueue fails
-- with "no such table" — at runtime, on exactly the devices that have been
-- using the app longest, and never on a freshly wiped one. That includes every
-- current test device.
--
-- Adding a migration also fixes the older columns retroactively: SQLDelight
-- derives the schema version from the migration COUNT, so shipping this bumps
-- the database to 2 and every future change now has a numbered home.
--
-- Kept identical to the declaration in `StationlyDatabase.sq`. The two are not
-- checked against each other (no `verifyMigrations`), so they drift silently.
CREATE TABLE ActivityEventEntity (
    id TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    uid TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    t INTEGER NOT NULL,
    props TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'
);

CREATE INDEX activity_by_time ON ActivityEventEntity(t);
